* Node: N11 (22nd round; R504 before). Round type: [check] of fresh material found by node-keyword arXiv API queries (submitted May–Nov 2026, ids not in our files; the same queries for N12, N13, N1, N5, N8, N9 found 2606.24405 (Berry–Keating review), 2608.14852 (short twisted second moment reciprocity, δ ∈ (1/2, 1)) and off-node papers), plus three exploration scouts.
* (1) 2605.24363 (23 May 2026), Thm 1.3 (main theorem-all-T, TeX l. 177–185, proof l. 535–564): for π ∈ F_m and fixed θ > 0, σ ≥ 1/2, sup_T T^{−2σθ} ∫_1^{T^θ} I_{y,π}(0,T) dy < ∞ ⇒ L(s,π) ≠ 0 for Re s > σ, where I_{y,π}(0,T) = ∫_0^T |M_{y,π}L(½+it,π)|² dt with the smoothed mollifier M_{x,π} log x = Σ_{n≤x} μ_π(n) n^{−s} log(x/n). HOLDS for a fixed zero ρ₀: the residue at w = ρ₀ + ½ − it gives x^{β₀+½}/((|γ₀−t|+1)²(|γ₀|+1)^{1+m}) ≪ ∫_1^x |M_y| log y dy, then Cauchy–Schwarz and the mean-square lower bound ∫|L|² ≫ T (Ji 2009, PAMS 137). Scout a1's FLAW ('pointwise Ramanujan bounds for μ_π') is wrong: l. 312–362 use only Luo–Rudnick–Sarnak's |α_{r,π}(p)| ≤ p^{δ_m}, δ_m ≤ 1/2 − 1/(m²+1), with |μ_π(n)| ≤ τ_m(n) n^{δ_m} (unconditional).
* (2) Cor 1.4 (cor:RH, l. 205–212) as printed (∃θ ∀ε: sup_T T^{−(1+ε)θ} ∫_1^{T^θ} I_y dy < ∞ ⇒ RH) has a hypothesis that fails for every θ < 2 already for ζ: M_y = 1 for 1 < y < 2 (eq:Mlogx), so ∫_1^2 I_y dy ≍ T log T, and for 2 ≤ y ≤ T^{1−δ} Cauchy–Schwarz with ∫_0^T ζM_y dt = T(1 + o(1)) gives I_y ≥ (1 − o(1))T, so ∫_1^{T^θ} I_y dy ≫ T^{1+min(θ,1−δ)}; for θ ≥ 2 it would force the mean of I_y over [T, T^θ] to be T^{o(1)}, against Farmer's θ = ∞ conjecture I_{T^θ} ~ T(1 + 1/θ) (l. 132–140). The paper's own remark (l. 214–224) computes that θ must grow as ε → 0: the intended form is ∀ε ∃θ, which follows from Thm 1.3 with σ = (1+ε)/2 (scout a2 agrees; orchestrator's reading of the TeX).
* (3) Thm 1.5 (main theorem-average, l. 250–262, proof l. 565–592: Σ_{π∈F} ∫_1^{T^θ} I_{y,π}(0,T) dy ≪ |F| T^{2σθ−δ} ⇒ N(σ,0,T;F)/|F| ≪ T^{−δ+ε}): the proof applies the fixed-zero lower bound ≫ x^{2β_π} + T/x (eq:lower-change-ave) to every π ∈ B, whose bad zeros may lie at any height γ_π ∈ [0, T], with constants depending on π; the uniform bound of the local proof (eq:main change in proof 2) is x^{2β}/T^{5+2m}, so the argument proves the family statement only with the extra factor T^{−5−2m} (as in the local Thm 1.1) and with constants uniform in π; F is allowed to be infinite (l. 235), where |F| is undefined. Unproved as stated (scout a3; orchestrator's reading). Not sent to REFUTATIONS: a conditional family criterion with a repairable exponent.
